From b7d91b71695544016b9e49f741a9b8b348dfc748 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Franco <gufranco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:01:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: recognise the Dungeon Master chip-free conversion

Dungeon Master is the only cartridge carrying a DSP-2. A conversion that
computes the chip's output ahead of time outgrows the 1 MB address space and
uses the same windowed layout the Star Ocean and Street Fighter conversions
already use, so it needs the same map.

Added to the title list with a comment saying which chip each entry removed,
since the list now covers more than one.

The size test does the safety work here. Retail Dungeon Master is 1,048,576
bytes, far below the 8 MB floor, so a stock dump cannot reach this branch and
still gets its DSP-2 from the chipset detection in ParseSNESHeader.
---
 memmap.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/memmap.cpp b/memmap.cpp
index a49f743f..b2cdb58f 100644
--- a/memmap.cpp
+++ b/memmap.cpp
@@ -2248,11 +2248,20 @@ void CMemory::InitROM (void)
 	Map_Initialize();
 	CalculatedChecksum = 0;
 
+	// Conversions whose graphics were expanded ahead of time and no longer need the
+	// coprocessor they were built around. Which chip each one removed does not affect
+	// the mapping: Star Ocean and the Street Fighter pair dropped an S-DD1, Dungeon
+	// Master drops a DSP-2.
+	//
+	// Every one of them is far larger than the retail cartridge it came from, so the
+	// size test keeps a stock dump from ever reaching this branch. Retail Dungeon
+	// Master is 1 MB and still takes the ordinary DSP detection above.
 	const bool8	WindowedLoROM = (CalculatedSize >= 0x800000) &&
 			(Settings.SDD1 ||
 			 strncmp(ROMName, "STREET FIGHTER ALPHA2", 21) == 0 ||
 			 strncmp(ROMName, "STREET FIGHTER ZERO2", 20) == 0 ||
-			 strncmp(ROMName, "Star Ocean", 10) == 0);
+			 strncmp(ROMName, "Star Ocean", 10) == 0 ||
+			 strncmp(ROMName, "DUNGEON MASTER", 14) == 0);
 
 	if (WindowedLoROM)
 	{
-- 
