From 5d7e5406c62a13743f9b18d1775e5a4b39983fb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Franco <gufranco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:02:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: map save RAM for windowed conversions that declare
 it

Map_WindowedLoROMMap gave every bank but $7E and $7F to ROM, which covers
both LoROM save RAM windows, and never called map_LoROMSRAM. Neither S-DD1
conversion carried save RAM so nothing had noticed. Dungeon Master carries
32 KB of battery-backed save RAM and is a game people play for tens of
hours.

Guarded on the image being 0x80 banks or fewer so the conversions that came
first are provably untouched: both are 0xC0 banks. At 0x80 banks or fewer
the loop already skips window banks $F0 to $FF, because $F0 would need image
bank 0x80 + 0x30 and that does not exist, so save RAM costs nothing there.

Banks $70 to $7D stay ROM in the loop, so a conversion declaring save RAM
has to keep its data out of them.
---
 memmap.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/memmap.cpp b/memmap.cpp
index b2cdb58f..87a4c4f9 100644
--- a/memmap.cpp
+++ b/memmap.cpp
@@ -4132,6 +4132,21 @@ void CMemory::Map_WindowedLoROMMap (void)
 		}
 	}
 
+	// Neither S-DD1 conversion carried save RAM, so this map never provided any and
+	// every bank above became ROM, including the two LoROM save RAM windows. Dungeon
+	// Master has 32 KB of battery-backed save RAM and cannot do without it.
+	//
+	// The size guard is what keeps this from disturbing the conversions that came
+	// first. At 0x80 banks or fewer, window bank $F0 needs image bank 0x80 + 0x30,
+	// which does not exist, so the loop above already skipped $F0 to $FF and save RAM
+	// costs nothing there. Larger images do map those window banks, and they are the
+	// ones this leaves alone.
+	//
+	// Banks $70 to $7D are ROM in the loop above, so a conversion that declares save
+	// RAM has to keep its data out of them.
+	if (SRAMSize > 0 && banks <= 0x80)
+		map_LoROMSRAM();
+
 	map_WRAM();
 	map_WriteProtectROM();
 }
-- 
2.55.0

